  "id": "subject-variable",
  "term": "subject variable",
  "definition": "A subject variable is a participant-based factor used to sort people into different groups for comparison in a study. In the source example, the number of mandatory running sessions served as a between-subject variable because different groups of students were compared on that basis.",
